# Ready-to-use requests for linking, selecting, renewing and revoking bank accounts.
# Works with the VS Code REST Client extension and with JetBrains HTTP client files.
# Replace the placeholder values below. Never commit a real key or a real connection or account key.

@host = https://ledger-api.example.com
@apiKey = paste-the-operator-key-here
@connectionKey = paste-a-connection-key-here
@accountKey = paste-an-account-key-here

### Start a link. Open the returned authorizationUrl in a browser on the home network or VPN and approve it in the bank app.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/bank/connections/link
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### List connections with their consent state and whole days left. Copy the connectionKey of the new connection.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/bank/connections
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### List the accounts of a connection. Nothing is synced until accounts are selected.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/bank/connections/{{connectionKey}}/accounts
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Select the accounts to sync and name them. Do this right after approving: the first sync starts now and reads the longest history.
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/bank/connections/{{connectionKey}}/accounts
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accounts": [
    { "accountKey": "{{accountKey}}", "displayName": "Joint", "sync": true }
  ]
}

### Sync now. The scheduler already syncs every morning, so this is only for fresh data in between. Add ?connectionKey=... when several connections are active.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/bank/sync
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Renew a connection that is expiring. Open the returned authorizationUrl and approve it again. History and selection are kept.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/bank/connections/{{connectionKey}}/renew
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Revoke a connection: the consent is ended at the provider and the connection is marked revoked.
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/bank/connections/{{connectionKey}}
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
